  "result": "`satisfies(version, range)` is now implemented in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (11 of 11).\n\nI added `test/satisfies.test.js` with 10 test groups covering these areas of the spec:\n- invalid input\n- version syntax\n- ordering\n- comparators and `||` sets\n- x-ranges\n- operators with partial versions\n- tilde, caret and hyphen ranges\n- the prerelease rule\n\nWhere the spec is silent I made these calls:\n- **Whitespace after an operator:** it is only accepted after `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` and `=`, as the spec lists. `~ 1.2.3` and `^ 1.2.3` return `false`.\n- **Hyphen ranges:** one only counts if it is the whole set, so `1.0.0 - 2.0.0 || 5.0.0` works but `>=1 1.0.0 - 2.0.0` is invalid.\n- **Prerelease identifiers:** one like `01` is accepted and compared as a number, because the spec only bans leading zeros in major, minor and patch.\n- **`>*` and `<*`:** these match nothing, while `>=*` and `<=*` match any non-prerelease version.\n\nMy first test run had five failures, caused by a bug in how I handled comparators with no operator. I fixed it and the suite now passes.",
